#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Entity Model"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unified Entity Model (v0.8)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:8
msgid ""
"FreeAnima stores most structured business data in a single **`entities`** "
"table. Self layer remains physically isolated in [`self_blocks`](self-"
"layer.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hierarchy: subject → world → content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer       | Entity type     | Role                                                |\n"
"| ----------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Subject** | `agent`, `user` | Who acts — exists **before** and **outside** worlds |\n"
"| **World**   | `world`         | Logical namespace / permission boundary             |\n"
"| **Content** | `content`       | Business data (tasks, future memory components, …)  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:18
msgid ""
"Subjects do **not** belong to a world. Each subject may have exactly **one "
"default private world** (exclusive, auto-created on subject creation). "
"Content belongs to a world via `world_id` and inherits that world's "
"visibility boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two orthogonal classifications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Layer           | Cardinality              | Purpose                                                    |\n"
"| --------------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Entity type** | 4 fixed values           | Architecture boundary: `content`, `world`, `agent`, `user` |\n"
"| **Components**  | Dynamic, many per entity | Functional markers: `task_list`, `task_item`, …            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:27
msgid ""
"Component fields live in **`body` JSONB** at the top level. "
"**`primary_component`** records the creation entry (usually immutable); list "
"views route by primary component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "`entities` table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Column                          | Role                                         |\n"
"| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `id`                            | `bigint` identity — global numeric ID        |\n"
"| `type`                          | One of four entity types                     |\n"
"| `world_id`                      | Native owning World (FK → `entities.id`)     |\n"
"| `components`                    | `text[]` component tags                      |\n"
"| `primary_component`             | Main component for module routing            |\n"
"| `title` / `summary` / `content` | Shared text columns (all components may use) |\n"
"| `body`                          | JSONB component payload                      |\n"
"| `created_at` / `updated_at`     | Timestamps                                   |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Not in v0.8 bootstrap:** relationship table, permission table, World nesting/mount, graph DB (PostgreSQL AGE).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subject (`agent` / `user`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:50
msgid ""
"Identity is **`type`** plus `agent_config` or `user_config` primary "
"component."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:50
msgid ""
"Subjects are **not** scoped by `world_id` in a membership sense; row "
"`world_id` stays at bootstrap root (`ENTITY_ROOT_WORLD_ID`) as a table "
"placeholder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:50
msgid ""
"**`agent_config` / `user_config` body**: `default_private_world_id` — the "
"subject's single default private world (auto-created on subject create; "
"configurable from private worlds owned by the subject)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:50
msgid ""
"**Notifications** use subject entity ids as `recipient_id` (see "
"[`notifications.md`](notifications.md) and `config.yaml` "
"`worlds.user_subject_id` / `agent_subject_id`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:50
msgid ""
"**Service API Token**（`service_api_tokens` 表）绑定 subject entity id；Hub "
"REST/SAP/MCP 从 Bearer token 解析调用方身份。见 [`remote-access.md`](../"
"guide/remote-access.md)。"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Boot-time ensure (`worlds` config)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:54
msgid ""
"Hub startup runs **`ensureWorldSubjects()`** once (after migrations, before "
"engine):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:59
msgid ""
"Ensures configured (or default `user=1` / `agent=2`) subject entities exist "
"with correct `type`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:59
msgid ""
"Ensures each subject has a **default private world** "
"(`default_private_world_id`); private world ids are **not fixed**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:59
msgid ""
"Binds **`ResolvedWorldContext`** in memory: `user_subject_id`, "
"`agent_subject_id`, `user_world_id`, `agent_world_id`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:59
msgid ""
"Type conflict (configured id exists but wrong `type`) **aborts service "
"startup**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:61
msgid ""
"Legacy SQL bootstrap seeds (public world id=1, Inbox id=2) are removed by "
"migration; default data is **code-owned**, not migration-seeded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "World namespace"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:70
msgid ""
"**`type: world`** entities are logical containers (permission/list boundary)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:70
msgid "Visibility and owner live in **`world_config` body**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:70
msgid "`private: false` — public world"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:70
msgid ""
"`private: true` + `owner_subject_id` — private world owned by an `agent` or "
"`user` entity"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:70
msgid ""
"`default_private: true` — marks the subject's **exclusive** default private "
"world (at most one per `owner_subject_id`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:70
msgid ""
"Do not confuse with semantic memory **`type=world`** (fact classification in "
"[`memory.md`](memory.md)) — that becomes `body.memory_kind=world` after "
"future migration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <messages><msg>
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:71 messages/po4a/en.xml:261
#: messages/po4a/en.xml:315
#, no-wrap
msgid "Content"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:75
msgid ""
"**`world_id`** is the sole namespace key; access boundary is inherited from "
"the owning world."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:75
msgid "Content entities do not store a separate owner column."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "Task module (first consumer)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:79
msgid "TickTick-style lists and items map to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:85
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept     | Entity         | Component      |\n"
"| ----------- | -------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| Task domain | `type=world`   | `world_config` |\n"
"| List        | `type=content` | `task_list`    |\n"
"| Item (task) | `type=content` | `task_item`    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:87
msgid ""
"Items reference their list via `body.list_id` (entity id). Task items store "
"**title** and **content** on entity columns; **tags** live in `body.tags`. "
"Each world gets a **default list** (`is_default: true`, name e.g.「收件箱」) "
"**lazily** on first task use (`ensureDefaultTaskListForWorld`); it cannot be "
"deleted or archived but may be renamed. List **`body.closed: true`** means "
"archived: hidden from the main sidebar by default (`tasklist.list` unless "
"`include_closed`), restorable via `tasklist.patch({ closed: false })`; "
"contained task items are kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:89
msgid ""
"Task/list tools and stores require explicit **`world_id`** (typically "
"`user_world_id` from system prompt / `GET /api/worlds/context`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Folders** (`body.is_folder: true`) are container nodes in the sidebar tree only — they cannot hold tasks directly (`task.create` / `task.patch` reject `list_id` pointing at a folder). Child lists and sub-folders reference a parent folder via `body.parent_id` (entity id of a folder, or omitted/null at root). Nesting must not form cycles. Archiving or deleting a folder cascades to descendants. `sort_order` is scoped among siblings sharing the same `parent_id`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:93
msgid ""
"LLM ToolSets: `@freeanima/capabilities-task` — `task` (item CRUD + "
"`task_search`) and `tasklist` (list CRUD + `tasklist_search`); load via "
"`toolset_load`. `task_search` searches all lists when `list_id` is omitted. "
"Legacy `tasks` table and `/api/tasks/*` are removed after one-time migration "
"([`scripts/archive/migrate-tasks-to-entities.ts`](../../scripts/archive/"
"migrate-tasks-to-entities.ts))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shell UI: global Subject scope"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:97
msgid ""
"Hub startup binds **`ResolvedWorldContext`** (`GET /api/worlds/context`). "
"The product shell exposes a **single User / Agent toggle** in the module "
"header — not an arbitrary `world_id` picker. Selection maps to "
"`user_world_id` / `agent_world_id` and persists in `sessionStorage` for the "
"tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Surface          | World binding                                    | Control                        |\n"
"| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n"
"| Shell header     | `user_world_id` or `agent_world_id`              | global **User / Agent** toggle |\n"
"| `/tasks`         | follows shell scope via SAP `subject_kind`       | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/email`         | follows shell scope via SAP `subject_kind`       | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/notifications` | `recipient_kind` + subject entity id             | none (inherits header)         |\n"
"| `/diary`         | subject default private world via `subject_kind` | none (inherits header)         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:107
msgid ""
"SAP task/email methods accept optional `subject_kind` (defaults: task "
"`user`, email `agent`). Satellites read the shell scope via "
"**`useSubjectScope()`** from `@freeanima/shell-sdk`; Hub REST entity search "
"uses **`resolveWorldIdForSubject()`** with the same scope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:109
msgid ""
"Future multi-world browse (e.g. diary calendar aggregation across worlds) "
"should add **module-scoped** filters or Admin tooling — not a speculative "
"arbitrary world picker."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Email module (Estate)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:113
msgid "Email accounts, threads, and mirrored messages map to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept | Entity         | Component       |\n"
"| ------- | -------------- | --------------- |\n"
"| Account | `type=content` | `email_account` |\n"
"| Thread  | `type=content` | `email_thread`  |\n"
"| Message | `type=content` | `email_message` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:121
msgid ""
"Accounts store SMTP/IMAP settings and sync cursor in `body.sync`. Messages "
"store IMAP UID in `body.imap_uid`; human-readable subject/body use entity "
"columns. IMAP sync upserts threads/messages; UI lives in shell `/email` (SAP "
"`email.*` methods), not Admin REST."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:123
msgid ""
"LLM ToolSets: `@freeanima/capabilities-email` — `email-account` (account "
"entities) and `email` (sync, send/receive, search); load via `toolset_load`. "
"Legacy `config.yaml` `email.accounts[]` migrates via [`scripts/archive/"
"migrate-email-to-entities.ts`](../../scripts/archive/migrate-email-to-"
"entities.ts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diary module"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:127
msgid "Structured journal entries for **user** and **agent** subjects:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:131
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Concept | Entity         | Component     |\n"
"| ------- | -------------- | ------------- |\n"
"| Entry   | `type=content` | `diary_entry` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:133
msgid ""
"Entries live in each subject's **`default_private_world_id`**. "
"`body.entry_at` is the timeline sort key; `title` / `summary` / `content` "
"use entity columns; optional `body.tags`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:137
msgid ""
"**SAP:** `diary.*` methods — all take `subject_kind: user | agent` "
"(including `diary.append`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:137
msgid "**UI:** shell `/diary` (`@freeanima/satellite-diary`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:137
msgid "**LLM:** ToolSet `diary` — agent private world only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:139
msgid "See [`docs/features/diary.md`](../features/diary.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <messages><msg>
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:140 messages/po4a/en.xml:116
#: messages/po4a/en.xml:128 messages/po4a/en.xml:556
#, no-wrap
msgid "Search"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:143
msgid ""
"Entity **list** (deterministic browse) and **search** (relevance ranking) "
"are separate ports:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:148
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Port                      | Role                                                                  |\n"
"| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `EntityStorePort.list`    | Structural filters; stable sort                                       |\n"
"| `EntitySearchPort.search` | Hard filters + optional text query; hybrid FTS/trigram/vector via RRF |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Scope:** default `world_id`; `global: true` requires an explicit accessible-world allowlist (public worlds only until subject permissions bootstrap).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:152
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Component filters:** whitelisted per `primary_component` (e.g. `task_item`: `status`, `list_id`, `tags`, `due_today`). Arbitrary JSONPath is forbidden.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:154
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Tools / API:** `entity_search` (LLM/MCP) and `GET|POST /api/entities/search` share `EntitySearchPort`. Task UI search box uses the same REST endpoint.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:156
msgid ""
"See memory hybrid search in [`memory.md`](memory.md) for FTS operator "
"syntax; entity search reuses the same query builder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "**FTS index:** same `fts_segmented` + jieba write path as semantic memory (`resolveFtsSegmentedForWrite` on entity create/update). Legacy rows imported before this column may lack segmentation; run Admin **FTS** rebuild (`onlyMissing`) to backfill `entities.fts_segmented` so jieba query tokens align with the GIN index.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:159
#, no-wrap
msgid "Future migration map (not executed yet)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:169
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Legacy table                 | Target                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `semantic_memory`            | `content` + memory component                                                                                               |\n"
"| `autobiographical_memory`    | `content` + narrative component                                                                                            |\n"
"| `limbic_memory`              | `content` + limbic component                                                                                               |\n"
"| `tasks` (legacy)             | `task_item` (when explicitly migrated)                                                                                     |\n"
"| `config.yaml email.accounts` | `email_account` (see [`scripts/archive/migrate-email-to-entities.ts`](../../scripts/archive/migrate-email-to-entities.ts)) |\n"
"| `memory_references`          | relationship table (future)                                                                                                |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/entity-model.md:170
msgid "See [`architecture.md`](architecture.md) for cognitive-layer context."
msgstr ""
